.claude
CLAUDE.md
# ⚠️ `.scratch/` HOLDS THE VILLA'S OWN VOCABULARY AND MUST NEVER BE TRACKED.
# `forbidden-tokens.txt` lists the property's name, hostname and model filename
# so `tests/hard-rules.py` can check they are absent from everything shipped —
# writing them into a tracked guard would BE the leak the guard exists to
# prevent. It was NOT ignored on this branch until 2.496.24, which was found by
# the guard's own first run trying to add its token list.
.scratch/
# ⚠️ `tests/*` AND NOT `tests/`, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE WHOLE POINT. Git
# cannot re-include anything whose PARENT directory is excluded, so `tests/`
# followed by `!tests/oracles/` silently keeps ignoring the whole tree — the
# negation never gets a chance to match. Matching the CHILDREN leaves the
# directory itself considered, so the negations below work.
#
# ⚠️ THIS BRANCH HAD THE BROKEN FORM UNTIL 2.496.23, AND IT IS WHY dev2 SHIPPED
# TO PRODUCTION WITH ONE GATE. Eighteen oracles existed and not one of them was
# tracked: a fresh clone had none, CI had none, and every pin written here was
# invisible the moment it left this machine.
tests/*
!tests/oracles/
!tests/consistency/
# ⚠️ THE PATTERN, NOT ONE FILE. This read `!tests/hard-rules.py` and git
# refused the very next guard added beside it. A negation naming one file is a
# negation somebody has to remember; naming the shape is one nobody does.
!tests/*.py
# ⚠️ AND THE DATA A GATE READS, NOT JUST THE GATE. `tests/forbidden-token-hashes.txt`
# is what lets the villa-name check run on a build server at all, and it landed
# here as a .txt — so `!tests/*.py` did not reach it, it was never committed,
# and CI failed on three consecutive releases with the check correctly refusing
# to pass without it. The lesson written three lines above, re-learned one
# extension over.
!tests/*.txt
# Local scratch inside the tracked directories stays ignored.
tests/oracles/*.log
tests/**/node_modules/
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
dist.zip
*.local
.env
.DS_Store
*.log
.vite
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
sources/
._*

# Local model & asset working files — these are user data, never committed.
*.sh3d
*.obj
*.mtl
*.glb

# Python bytecode (supervisor-proxy.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local dev TLS certs (mkcert) — never commit
certs/
